  "inspection": {
    "question": "What is the bolt circle diameter, and where did that number come from?",
    "answered": true,
    "answer": "The NEMA\u202f23 mounting standard defines a square bolt pattern whose side length is **47.14\u202fmm**. Treating that square as a circular bolt circle, the distance from the centre of the pattern to each hole (the radius) is half the diagonal of the square:\n\n\\[\n\\text{radius} = \\frac{47.14}{\\sqrt{2}} \\approx 33.27\\text{\u202fmm}\n\\]\n\nso the **bolt\u2011circle diameter** is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{diameter} = 2 \\times 33.27 \\approx 66.5\\text{\u202fmm}\n\\]\n\nThis value comes directly from the NEMA\u202f23 stepper\u2011mount specification retrieved by the `lookup_standard` tool (source: \u201cNEMA\u202f23 stepper mount: 47.14\u202fmm square bolt pattern \u2026\u201d).\n\nThe current CAD model does not contain any cylindrical faces, so the bolt\u2011circle pattern (and its 4\u202f\u00d7\u202fM5 clearance holes) is not yet implemented in the part. The verification report flagged this as a failure: \u201cmounting hole pattern exists in the built solid \u2013 the solid contains none.\u201d",
    "error": null,
    "model": "fallback:k2think",
    "inspected": true,
    "tools_used": [
      "lookup_standard"
    ],
    "tool_calls": [
      {
        "tool": "lookup_standard",
        "arguments": {
          "query": "NEMA 23 bolt circle diameter"
        },
        "ok": true,
        "observation": "- NEMA 23 stepper mount: 47.14 mm square bolt pattern (5.1 mm holes (M5 clearance)), pilot boss \u00f838.1 mm, shaft \u00f86.35 mm, faceplate 56.4 mm square",
        "duration_ms": 10.2,
        "raw_keys": [
          "results"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rounds": 1,
    "explain_ms": 5344.7
  },
